course: dictionary
lesson: 4697
title: Honestly: three meanings in one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Honestly» is a small word with big jobs. Read the words around it to find which job it is doing. The clues are in the sentence, not in the word itself.
explain: First, it means in an honest way: without lying, cheating or stealing. «If you lose or damage a library book, you tell the librarian honestly.» Here the child does not hide the mistake.
explain: Second, it shows you are telling the truth or giving your real opinion: «Honestly, I didn't take it.» Maddie also uses it this way: «Maddie honestly hadn't noticed.» Check by asking: is the speaker promising that their words are true?
explain: Third, it can show you are annoyed or surprised, as in «Oh, honestly!» The tone and the words before it tell you which feeling it is. Remember that people sometimes say «honestly» to make a claim sound more convincing, so it does not always prove that something is true.
fact: Honestly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done or said.
fact: «Honestly» can mean without lying, cheating or stealing, as in «answer honestly».
fact: «Honestly» can mean telling the truth, as in «to be honest» or «honestly speaking».
fact: «Oh, honestly!» is an exclamation that shows you are annoyed or surprised.
fact: «No cap» (young slang) means honestly, so «no cap» and «honestly» can mean the same thing.
exercise: «Honestly, I didn't take it.» What does honestly show here? | *The speaker is telling the truth | The speaker is lost in the library | The speaker is cheating at a game | The speaker is very hungry
exercise: In a game, what does playing honestly mean? | Changing the rules when you are losing | Making up your own score | Hiding the ball so nobody finds it | *Following the rules
exercise: Mum says, «Oh, honestly!» when the cat knocks over her cup. What does it show? | *She is annoyed | She is stealing the cup | She is very hungry | She is telling a lie about the cup
test: «If you lose or damage a library book, you tell the librarian honestly.» What does honestly mean here? | Quickly and loudly | *Without lying, hiding nothing | Not at all, never | Angrily, with a shout
test: What does «no cap» mean in young slang? | Sir or Miss | *Honestly | Hidden away | Brother or mate
exam: Why might a hurt friend say «I'm fine, honestly»? | They are very hungry and want lunch | *They are embarrassed and do not want a fuss | They want to go to the library | They have finished their homework early
